{"availability":"available","full":"warner-wvez/Ora","name":"Ora","description":"A live map of every public traffic camera in the US: about 46,100 cameras across 49 states, with real live video where the state DOT allows it.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-08T21:44:47Z","updated":"2026-10-16T21:43:38Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://warner-wvez.github.io/Ora/","topics":["data-pipeline","gis","github-pages","hls","maplibre","open-data","python","static-site","traffic-cameras","transportation"],"demo":"https://warner-wvez.github.io/Ora/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:50:12.472Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T23:50:12.472Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T23:50:12.472Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:25:57.174Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T06:12:50.575Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-12T02:04:54.836Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T23:50:12.472Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A live map of every public traffic camera in the United States.","Pick a state, click a pin, and see what that camera sees right now. Where the state transportation department allows it, the popup plays the real live stream; everywhere else it shows the agency's refreshing snapshot and says so. A camera that is not actually showing a road gets a grey pin, because a six-hour sweep checks every one. No account, no server, no build step: one HTML file, one JSON file per state, and the agencies' own feeds."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/warner-wvez/Ora/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e162e75e97951b1ea70d6ef6f98aa69ac6a107f225b63cb8b01761890789bb31","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:25:57.325Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:50:12.557Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A live map of every public traffic camera in the United States.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/warn